TEXT 48 -368 Left 3 ;#105 Three-transistor sawtooth generator
TEXT 48 -304 Left 2 ;Source: Alan Wolke (W2AEW), https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2a1I1X3RV0g
TEXT 48 -256 Left 2 ;A PNP current source charges 10nF; a regenerative PNP-NPN pair quickly discharges it when the threshold is crossed.
TEXT 1520 -352 Left 2 !.ic V(RAMP)=0
TEXT 1520 -304 Left 2 !.tran 0 20m 0 100n
TEXT 1520 -232 Left 2 !.meas tran RAMP_MIN MIN V(RAMP) FROM 5m TO 20m
TEXT 1520 -192 Left 2 !.meas tran RAMP_MAX MAX V(RAMP) FROM 5m TO 20m
TEXT 1520 -152 Left 2 !.meas tran T1 WHEN V(RAMP)=2 RISE=4
TEXT 1520 -112 Left 2 !.meas tran T2 WHEN V(RAMP)=2 RISE=5
TEXT 1520 -72 Left 2 !.meas tran PERIOD PARAM T2-T1
TEXT 1520 -32 Left 2 !.meas tran FREQ PARAM 1/(T2-T1)
TEXT 1520 8 Left 2 !.meas tran TR_LO WHEN V(RAMP)=1.5 RISE=4
TEXT 1520 48 Left 2 !.meas tran TR_HI WHEN V(RAMP)=4.5 RISE=4
TEXT 1520 88 Left 2 !.meas tran RAMP_SLOPE PARAM 3/(TR_HI-TR_LO)
TEXT 1520 128 Left 2 !.meas tran ICHARGE PARAM 10n*3/(TR_HI-TR_LO)
TEXT 1520 168 Left 2 !.meas tran VBIAS AVG V(BIAS) FROM 5m TO 20m
TEXT 1520 240 Left 2 ;Values are shown in Alan's video at 0:40 to 1:44.\nThe transistor types are simulation choices;\nAlan does not name them in the drawing.
TEXT 1520 368 Left 2 ;ICHARGE derives the charging current from the ramp\nslope, as C times dV/dt, so it can be compared with\nthe roughly 30 uA Alan quotes.
